The only method that is required to be overwritten is the \lstinline{k()} feedback method on \cref{line:pid_gpu_k} but as PIDs require some history to calculate the $i$ and $d$ portions, we request extra memory by setting the \lstinline{SHARED_MEM_REQUEST_BLK_BYTES} variable on \cref{line:pid_shared_mem}.
This variable allows for extra shared memory per trajectory sample which is necessary for keeping track of history on the GPU.
