\paragraph{Contributions} 
We summarize our contributions.
\begin{itemize}
 \item In the setting of WFAs over the max-plus semiring, we find that the WFA learning algorithm in~\cite{DBLP:conf/fossacs/HeerdtKR020} can return hypothesis automata that are unfaithful to previous membership queries (\S{}\ref{subsec:HeerdtEtAlDoesNotWork}).
 \item We introduce the notion of \emph{column-closedness} that replaces consistency. We also present a WFA learning algorithm based on it, which works for an arbitrary semiring. We prove that the learned WFA is always faithful (\S{}\ref{sec:columnClosedness}).
 \item We compared Van Heerdt's algorithm, our algorithm, and Balle's algorithm, and gave a unifying overview of when automata learning on general semirings proceeds correctly without stalling, based on the concept of column-closedness (\S{}\ref{subsec:HeerdtEtAlDoesNotWork}).
