\subsection{Basic Mechanism of Dumping GPU Buffers}
\label{sec:ckpt-dumping}

Dumping active GPU buffers to host memory is periodically conducted in POS, and the interval between dumpings is configurable by the operator according to different SLO requirements on C/R (see \TODO{}). Similar to current optimizations on CPU-side checkpoint, POS seperates the dumping process into \ding{182} \textit{pre-copy} and \ding{183} \textit{delta-copy} phases. 
During the first phase, POS overlaps the copying of GPU memory with normal kernel execution. The overlapping hides the copy overhead without interfering with the execution of kernels, as modern GPU hardware has independent computation engine and copy engine (\eg over PCIe DMA, RDMA and other specialized buses such as NVLink).
