\subsection{Concurrent C/R execution}
\label{sec:design-features}

\noindent
{\sys} concurrently executes the C/R with GPU execution to hide the C/R costs. 
To ensure correctness, we retrofit the following classic CPU techniques in software for the GPU
with the help of the kernel DAG.
This section first describes the common cases when the DAG generated with speculation is correct, 
and then elaborate on the fallback path. 

