%  \begin{equation}
%            \frac{\rho g}{\sigma} < \beta.
%\end{equation}
%The critical value $\beta$ depends on all the data, including the loads, which makes it impractical to determine explicitly.  

%However, its lower bounds $\tilde{\beta}$ can be proposed. For instance, considering the theoretical scenario where the whole boundary of the horizontal domain acts as full-pin support (and that each node connects to the boundary points by a member), one can put $\tilde{\beta} = \frac{\pi}{D}$, where $D$ is the diameter of the largest circle that can be inscribed into the domain. Namely, ensuring that $\frac{\rho g}{\sigma} D < \pi$ would guarantee that the two assumptions are met, although this criterium may turn out conservative for some load cases.

