\section{Limitations of the Bhakti Database}

Despite the numerous advantages of the Bhakti database, it is not without limitations. The lightweight nature of Bhakti, while beneficial for small to medium-sized datasets, reveals some constraints when scaling up to larger data volumes. Here, we discuss the primary limitations of Bhakti:

\paragraph{Performance with Large Datasets} One of the most significant limitations of Bhakti is its performance with large datasets. As demonstrated in my testing on different scales of data, Bhakti's query times begin to increase sharply beyond approximately 4000 data entries. This increase indicates that while Bhakti is effective for smaller datasets, it may not be the optimal solution for applications requiring high throughput or handling very large datasets.

\paragraph{Lack of Approximate Calculation Methods} Bhakti currently focuses on precise computations rather than approximate methods like Hierarchical Navigable Small World (HNSW) \cite{Bentley1975}. This focus means that for applications where speed is critical, and approximate results are acceptable, Bhakti may not perform as well as databases designed for approximate nearest neighbor search.

\paragraph{Limited Support for Complex Queries} Bhakti's domain-specific language (DSL) for document-based pattern matching pre-filtering is a powerful feature, but it may not support all the complex query operations that more robust vector database solutions offer. This limitation could affect the flexibility of the system in handling intricate data retrieval and analysis tasks.

\paragraph{Scalability Concerns} While the Bhakti system is designed with a client-server model that allows for independent scaling of components, its scalability in a real-world, large-scale production environment has not been extensively tested. The separation of concerns between the client, server, and storage engine, while beneficial for maintenance and upgrades, may present challenges when scaling to meet the demands of a high-volume, enterprise-level application.

