%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

\section{Conclusion}
This study introduces an Evolutionary Diffusion-based Neural Architecture Generation Approach, called EDNAG, an efficient neural architecture generation method without networks. 
We propose a fitness-guided denoising strategy (FD) that maps fitness to probabilistic space, thereby guiding the DDIM-based denoising process for architecture generation. 
Extensive experiments demonstrate that EDNAG achieves SOTA performance in generating task-optimal architectures and surpasses existing baselines in generation efficiency and computational cost. 
We believe that EDNAG will contribute significantly to the development of NAS by reducing computational costs and accelerating practical application.

