Compared methods encompasses both streamable~\cite{sun20243dgstream, gao2024hicom} and non-streamable~\cite{wu20244d, yang2023real, luiten2024dynamic} works. 
Performance evaluation incorporates two key items: PSNR values of the test view to assess rendering quality, and overall model size to measure representation compactness. 
For streamable methods~\cite{sun20243dgstream, gao2024hicom}, we report per-frame model size to facilitate a direct comparison of compression efficiency.
Meanwhile, results of methods~\cite{sun20243dgstream, gao2024hicom} are adopted from HiCoM~\cite{gao2024hicom} since our experimental setup rigorously mirrors their method.

