In this figure, the solid and dashed magenta curves for respective dual- and single-threaded execution of the $ O \left( kn \log n \right) + O \left( n \log n \right) $ algorithm are separated by one $ \log_2 $ unit in the $y$-coordinate. This $y$-separation in log space corresponds to multiplication in linear space, so dual-threaded execution exhibits twice as many LLC load misses as single-threaded execution. Similarly, the green and red curves reveal that dual- or single-threaded execution of the $ O \left( n \log n \right) $ or $ O \left( kn \log n \right) $ algorithm exhibits far fewer LLC load misses than the $ O \left( kn \log n \right) + O \left( n \log n \right) $ algorithm.

