where $\psi_{i}(t) \geq 0$, $\boldsymbol \pi_i(t) \geq 0$, $\boldsymbol \alpha =(\alpha(0), \dots, \alpha({T-1}))^\top$, $\boldsymbol \delta =(\boldsymbol\delta^\top(0), \dots, \boldsymbol\delta^\top({T-1}))^\top$,  $\boldsymbol\Psi_i =(\psi_{i}(0), \dots, \psi_{i}(T-1))^\top$, and $ {\boldsymbol\Psi} = ( {\boldsymbol\Psi}_1^\top, \dots,  {\boldsymbol\Psi}_N^\top)^\top$. We define $\boldsymbol\Pi_i$ and  $\boldsymbol\Pi$  in a similar way. 
