   $,
   which satisfies $\boldsymbol l_i^\star(t) \leq \mathbf w_i^\ast(t)-\mathbf g_i(p_i^\star(t))$ and $\sum_{i=1}^N \boldsymbol l_i^\star(t)=0$. Select $\mathbf L_i^\star=(\boldsymbol l_i^{\star\top}(0), \cdots, \boldsymbol l_i^{\star\top}(T-1))^\top$ and $\mathbf L^\star=(\mathbf L_1^{\star\top}, \cdots, \mathbf L_N^{\star\top})^\top$. By contradiction, suppose $(\mathbf U^\star, \mathbf P^\star, \mathbf L^\star)$ does not maximize \eqref{eq2}. Then there exists $(\overline{\mathbf U}^\star, \overline{\mathbf P}^\star, \overline{\mathbf L}^\star)$ that satisfies the constraints in \eqref{eq2} and
